==Icelandic==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|is|non|dúkr}}, borrowed from {{der|is|gml|dôk}}, {{m|is|gml|dûk}}, from {{der|is|osx|dōk}}, from. {{der|is|gmw-pro|*dōk||cloth, rag}}, from {{der|is|gem-pro|*dōkaz||cloth, rag}}, from {{der|is|ine-pro|*dʰwōg-||cloth}}

Cognate with {{cog|da|dug}}, {{cog|sv|duk}}, {{cog|nn|duk}}, {{cog|nb|duk}}, and {{cog|de|Tuch}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|is|/ˈtuːkʏr/}}
* {{rhymes|is|uːkʏr|s=2}}

===Noun===
{{is-noun|m|dúks|dúkar}}

# [[cloth]], [[sheet]] (usually fabric, but also refers to things like e.g. [[linoleum]] flooring)

